# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values you need. `docker compose` reads `.env` from this
# directory automatically, so `docker compose run --rm runner ...` picks these up without
# exporting them by hand. Running the CLI directly with `uv run` (see src/runner/README.md)
# still needs them exported into your shell, e.g. `export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)`.

# Required for `casev run` (not needed for `casev validate`/`score`).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. Only needed when running the CLI directly with `uv run` — `docker compose` sets
# this to /dataset itself via the volume mount in docker-compose.yml.
# CASEV_DATASET_DIR=/path/to/dataset

# Optional. `casev run --model <slug>` works for any model regardless of the roster; this only
# overrides the max-px cap for a *listed* model (so you don't need --max-px yourself) and, as a
# GitHub Actions repo Variable, which models the weekly benchmark workflow runs. A JSON object
# of the same shape as MODEL_ROSTER in src/runner/core/config.py (slug -> max long-edge px).
# CASEV_MODEL_ROSTER={"vendor/model-x": 5000}
